{"asked":[{"category":"roles","id":"Q-1","impact":3,"impactReason":"Decides who can see which orders and invoices.","options":["No Account Manager role in release 1; every buyer sees all orders and invoices of their own company","Include the Account Manager role; buyers see only orders they placed, Account Managers see the whole company","No Account Manager role; buyers see only the orders they placed themselves"],"reason":"Matches the buyer capabilities as written ('their company's orders') with one fewer role to build.","recommended":"No Account Manager role in release 1; every buyer sees all orders and invoices of their own company","score":9,"spans":["I-5","I-9","I-15","I-17"],"text":"Is the Customer Account Manager role part of the first release, and if not, which company-level views do buyers get?","topic":"roles","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-2","impact":3,"impactReason":"Affects the payment status customers and staff see.","options":["Due date = invoice date + one configurable payment-terms number of days; Unpaid becomes Overdue after that","Payment terms set per customer company","No Overdue logic in release 1"],"reason":"The smallest rule that still supports the required Overdue status.","recommended":"Due date = invoice date + one configurable payment-terms number of days; Unpaid becomes Overdue after that","score":9,"spans":["I-16","I-5"],"text":"How is an invoice's Overdue status worked out?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"roles","id":"Q-3","impact":3,"impactReason":"Decides who can change delivery data.","options":["No; addresses are managed by staff/admin and customers only choose one","Yes, any buyer can","Only Account Managers can"],"reason":"The smallest option, and it keeps addresses under the distributor's control.","recommended":"No; addresses are managed by staff/admin and customers only choose one","score":6,"spans":["I-13","I-17"],"text":"Can customers create or edit their own delivery addresses?","uncertainty":2},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-4","impact":3,"impactReason":"Changes invoice money amounts.","options":["Prices are net; the invoice adds one configurable tax rate and shows the tax line","Prices include tax; invoices show no tax breakdown","No tax handling in release 1"],"reason":"B2B invoices normally show tax, and one rate keeps it simple.","recommended":"Prices are net; the invoice adds one configurable tax rate and shows the tax line","score":6,"spans":["I-11","I-16"],"text":"Are prices and invoice totals tax-exclusive, and is tax shown on invoices?","uncertainty":2},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-5","impact":3,"impactReason":"Decides what history data is written.","options":["One generic audit log entry per change (who, when, entity, field before/after), viewable by admins","Separate history tables for each entity type","Record status changes only"],"reason":"The simplest model that covers every entity I-8 names.","recommended":"One generic audit log entry per change (who, when, entity, field before/after), viewable by admins","score":6,"spans":["I-8"],"text":"How should changes to catalogue items and customer accounts be recorded?","topic":"audit","uncertainty":2}],"assumptions":[{"fromQuestion":"Q-2","fromSpan":["I-13","I-15"],"id":"ASM-1","risk":"low","text":"Saved basket templates (section 16) are in the request but in none of the listed goals. Are they in scope for this build? → assumed: Out of scope for this build; repeat order covers re-ordering"},{"fromDefault":"reporting","fromQuestion":"Q-3","fromSpan":["I-7"],"id":"ASM-2","risk":"low","text":"What does 'basic sales and product reporting' for management cover beyond the staff dashboard counts? → assumed: On-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder."},{"fromQuestion":"Q-4","fromSpan":["I-3","I-11"],"id":"ASM-3","risk":"high","text":"How should a product with no price on the customer's assigned price list be shown? → assumed: Show it with 'Price on request' and block adding it to the basket"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-5","fromSpan":["I-3","I-12"],"id":"ASM-4","risk":"low","text":"Where does the 'low stock' quantity threshold come from? → assumed: One system-wide threshold that admins can change in system settings"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-6","fromSpan":["I-12"],"id":"ASM-5","risk":"high","text":"If an ERP CSV contains product identifiers the portal doesn't recognise, what should the import do? → assumed: Apply the matching rows, skip and list the unknown identifiers, and mark the import as succeeded with warnings"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-7","fromSpan":["I-12"],"id":"ASM-6","risk":"low","text":"How does the nightly ERP CSV reach the portal? → assumed: The ERP drops the file into a configured folder or SFTP location that the portal reads on a schedule"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-8","fromSpan":["I-3","I-13"],"id":"ASM-7","risk":"high","text":"Can a customer order more than the imported stock quantity of an in-stock or low-stock product? → assumed: No; the order is limited to the imported quantity, and out-of-stock products can't be added"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-9","fromSpan":["I-13"],"id":"ASM-8","risk":"low","text":"Which timezone and which non-working days apply to the 14:00 delivery cutoff? → assumed: One configured business timezone, with weekends plus an admin-maintained list of holiday dates as non-working days"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-13","fromSpan":["I-14"],"id":"ASM-9","risk":"low","text":"Does a staff rejection need its own 'Rejected' status? → assumed: No; a rejection becomes Cancelled with a stored reason"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-14","fromSpan":["I-10","I-17"],"id":"ASM-10","risk":"low","text":"Are categories flat or nested? → assumed: Flat, one level"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-15","fromSpan":["I-9","I-17"],"id":"ASM-11","risk":"low","text":"How long do password-reset links and invitation links last, and can invitations be resent? → assumed: Configurable expiry (default 1 hour for reset, 7 days for invitations); admins can resend an invitation, which cancels the old link"},{"fromDefault":"sign-in","fromQuestion":"Q-16","fromSpan":["I-9"],"id":"ASM-12","risk":"low","text":"Can a user who is locked out request a password reset? → assumed: Email and password, with a reset link by email; no social or single sign-on."},{"fromQuestion":"Q-18","fromSpan":["I-13"],"id":"ASM-13","risk":"low","text":"Does the basket persist across sessions and devices? → assumed: Saved per user on the server, kept across sessions"},{"fromDefault":"notifications","fromQuestion":"Q-19","fromSpan":["I-14","I-1"],"id":"ASM-14","risk":"low","text":"Who receives order emails (confirmation, amendment, rejection, out for delivery), including for staff-created orders? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push."},{"fromQuestion":"Q-20","fromSpan":["I-2","I-10","I-17"],"id":"ASM-15","risk":"low","text":"Where does vehicle compatibility data come from? → assumed: Admins enter it by hand per product in the portal"},{"fromDefault":"data-migration","fromQuestion":"Q-21","fromSpan":["I-10","I-11","I-17"],"id":"ASM-16","risk":"high","text":"Do existing customers, products, prices or past orders need to be loaded before go-live? → assumed: No; the system starts empty, with seed data for set-up."},{"fromQuestion":"Q-22","fromSpan":["I-9","I-17"],"id":"ASM-17","risk":"high","text":"What happens to users and orders when a customer company is set to inactive? → assumed: Its users can't sign in or order; history is kept and visible to staff"},{"fromQuestion":"Q-23","fromSpan":["I-5","I-16"],"id":"ASM-18","risk":"low","text":"Should the customer invoice list only ever contain invoices for Delivered orders? → assumed: Yes; invoices exist only from Delivered onwards, and orders not yet delivered show no invoice"}],"conflicts":["Section 3.1 gives buyers 'View their company's orders', but section 3.2 lists 'View orders placed by other users within the same company' as an extra Account Manager capability. These contradict each other about what buyers can see (see Q-1).","Section 16 specifies saved basket templates and the buyer capabilities include 'Save baskets as templates', but no intent span covers templates (see Q-2)."],"differences":[{"id":"D-1.1","readings":[{"behaviour":5,"sketch":3,"summary":"Invoice is only viewable once order reaches Delivered status (since invoice is created at that point)"},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":1,"summary":"Customer views list of invoices and opens invoice detail with payment status without restriction on order status"},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Customer can view a list of invoices with payment status (paid/unpaid/overdue) without restriction on order status"}],"span":"I-5","topic":"Invoice viewing availability"}],"round":1,"sketches":[{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can sign in, browse catalogue, build a basket, and submit an order entirely through the web portal without phoning or emailing the office."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each self-service order creates an order record with an order number, replacing a manual order-entry log."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can still create orders on behalf of customers for phone-in cases, but system flags these as staff-created."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the portal is unavailable, there is no automatic fallback - customers would need to contact the office directly (out of scope for the system itself)."}],"id":"I-1","readingChosen":"Portal fully replaces phone/email ordering as the primary channel for placing orders; customers self-serve end-to-end from browsing to order placement without staff phone/email intervention."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer enters a full or partial product name and sees matching products."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer enters a full or partial part number/product code and sees matching products."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer enters a manufacturer part number and sees matching products."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer selects a category and sees only products in that category; can change or clear the category filter."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer selects vehicle attributes (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) and sees products marked compatible with that vehicle."},{"kind":"data","text":"Search and vehicle-filter results reflect only active (non-retired) products."},{"kind":"error","text":"Search with no matches returns an empty result state rather than an error."},{"kind":"error","text":"Vehicle search with no compatible products shown informs the customer none are found."}],"id":"I-2","readingChosen":"Search/filter is multi-faceted: by part number/code, by product name, by category, and by vehicle details (make/model/year/engine/fuel/variant)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Catalogue list, product detail, basket, and checkout all display the price from the price list assigned to the signed-in customer's company."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Product shows stock status of In stock, Low stock, or Out of stock, derived from the latest successful ERP import."},{"kind":"permission","text":"A buyer cannot view pricing associated with any other customer company."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a product has no price in the customer's assigned price list, the product's price is not shown as if it were free/zero (treated as unavailable/needs admin fix) rather than silently defaulting."},{"kind":"data","text":"Order-time price is captured and stored on the order line independent of later price-list changes."}],"id":"I-3","readingChosen":"Each customer, wherever pricing/stock appears (catalogue list, product detail, basket, checkout, order), sees the price from their assigned price list and current stock status, never another customer's pricing."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Orders placed by customers arrive directly in the staff order queue without staff needing to type them in from a phone call or email."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can confirm an order with validation of stock/customer info in a single action rather than manual re-entry."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can amend quantities/lines/delivery details on an existing order rather than recreating it from scratch."},{"kind":"data","text":"Staff-created orders (phone-in) are flagged as staff-created and auditable, distinguishing manual entries from self-service ones."}],"id":"I-4","readingChosen":"Reduce office staff manual order-entry by having customers enter orders themselves; staff only need to review/confirm/edit rather than re-key orders from phone/email."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer views list of their company's orders with order number, date, delivery date, address, total, status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer opens an order detail page showing status timeline (status, date/time, who/what performed transition)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer views list of invoices and opens invoice detail with payment status (Paid/Unpaid/Overdue)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer downloads invoice as PDF."},{"kind":"permission","text":"A buyer cannot view orders or invoices belonging to another customer company."}],"id":"I-5","readingChosen":"Customers can view the status/timeline of their own orders and view/download their own invoices with payment status."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff view an order queue listing order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, total, and current status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff filter the queue by customer, date, and status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff open an order from the queue to view/edit/confirm/reject it."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff export today's delivery list as a CSV containing order number, customer, delivery address, contact info, delivery date, lines/summary, notes, and delivery status."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only office staff and administrators can access the order queue and delivery export, not customers."}],"id":"I-6","readingChosen":"Staff see an operational queue of orders (filterable) and can export delivery information for drivers."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff dashboard shows counts/lists of new orders, orders awaiting confirmation, orders in picking, orders out for delivery, today's deliveries, outstanding invoices, and failed ERP imports."},{"kind":"data","text":"Reporting data is derived from stored order, invoice, and stock-import records rather than manually compiled."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only office staff/admin roles can view the dashboard and reports, not customers."}],"id":"I-7","readingChosen":"Management-facing reporting is delivered via a staff dashboard with operational/sales/product counts; detailed report types are open/minimal for first release."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Each order status transition is recorded with status, date/time, and user/system that performed it, retained as a timeline."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each invoice payment recording stores payment date and the user who recorded it."},{"kind":"data","text":"Staff amendments to an order (quantity/line/date/address/note changes) are stored as an audit history on the order."},{"kind":"data","text":"Catalogue changes (admin add/edit/retire of products, categories, prices) are recorded for administrative history viewing."},{"kind":"data","text":"Deactivating a user does not delete their historical order/invoice records; they remain visible to admins/staff."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Administrators can view administrative/audit history information for these changes."}],"id":"I-8","readingChosen":"The system records an immutable audit trail: who/when for order status transitions, invoice payment recording, customer account changes, and catalogue (product/price/category) changes."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"User signs in with email and password and is granted a session; incorrect credentials show an invalid-credentials message without revealing which field was wrong."},{"kind":"error","text":"Sign-in attempt for an inactive/deactivated account is blocked with an account-status message."},{"kind":"happy","text":"User signs out, ending their session."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Unauthenticated users cannot access any protected pages (catalogue, basket, orders, invoices, admin) and are redirected to sign-in."},{"kind":"happy","text":"User requests password reset via email; receives reset email with link; sets new password; can then sign in with new password."},{"kind":"error","text":"Invalid or expired reset link is rejected with an error message."},{"kind":"error","text":"After 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, the account is locked for 15 minutes, with further attempts blocked and the user informed of the temporary lock; successful sign-in after lock period restores normal access."},{"kind":"permission","text":"A deactivated user cannot sign in and cannot place new orders, but their historical orders/invoices remain visible to staff/admin."}],"id":"I-9","readingChosen":"Full authentication lifecycle: sign-in with email/password, forgot-password flow with emailed reset link, and account management including lockout and deactivation handling."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Each product record stores name, internal ID, manufacturer part number, distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit of sale, pack size, image, active/retired status, and compatibility links."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer browses a paginated/listed catalogue showing image, name, code, manufacturer, unit/pack size, price, stock status, and add-to-basket control per product."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin creates, edits, and retires categories; assigns products to categories."},{"kind":"data","text":"Retired products no longer appear in catalogue browsing/search but remain intact in historical orders."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer searches/filters as described in I-2 behaviours (name, code, manufacturer part number, brand, category, vehicle)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Product detail page shows image, name, code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, price, stock status, vehicle compatibility list, quantity selector, add-to-basket."}],"id":"I-10","readingChosen":"Build the product catalogue data model and browsing UI: product fields, categories (flat, admin-managed), search, filters, and vehicle-compatibility matching."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin creates a price list and names it."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin adds products to a price list and sets a price for each."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin edits an existing product's price within a price list."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin removes a product from a price list."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin assigns a price list to a customer company and can change the assignment later."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin deactivates a price list, preventing its further assignment/use for display."},{"kind":"data","text":"Changing a customer's price-list assignment or editing prices does not alter prices already stored on existing orders."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a product has no price entry in the customer's assigned price list, the product is treated as unpriced/unavailable for that customer rather than shown with a default price."}],"id":"I-11","readingChosen":"One price per product per price list; admin manages price lists and assigns them to customers; customer sees only their assigned list's prices."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A scheduled job ingests the nightly ERP CSV, validates the file format and product identifiers, and updates stock quantities/status (In stock/Low stock/Out of stock) for matching products."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each import run records a success or failure outcome with timestamp, visible to staff/admin."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the CSV is invalid or incomplete, the import is rejected, the previous valid stock data remains in effect, and the failure is logged and visible to staff/admin (e.g. on dashboard)."},{"kind":"permission","text":"The portal never writes stock data back to the ERP; it only reads/imports the file."},{"kind":"happy","text":"After a successful import, the catalogue and product pages reflect the newly imported stock status immediately."}],"id":"I-12","readingChosen":"Stock availability is driven solely by a nightly ERP CSV import process; portal is read-only with respect to ERP stock, and import failures are handled gracefully."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer adds a product to basket, changes line quantity, or removes a line; basket shows line price, line total, and subtotal."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Basket persists while the customer navigates the site within their session."},{"kind":"happy","text":"At checkout, customer selects one of their company's eligible delivery addresses and an available delivery date computed per the cutoff rule (before 14:00 -> next working day; at/after 14:00 -> the working day after next), excluding configured non-working days."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer adds an optional order note before submitting."},{"kind":"happy","text":"System re-validates stock and prices at checkout before allowing submission, showing the final reviewed order before confirming."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a basket item becomes out of stock or its price has changed before checkout completes, the customer is shown the updated status/price before they can submit."},{"kind":"happy","text":"On successful submission, an order number is generated, order-time prices are stored, status is set to Received, and the customer sees a confirmation."}],"id":"I-13","readingChosen":"Basket add/edit/remove plus a checkout flow enforcing the 14:00 cutoff delivery-date rule, address/date selection, stock/price validation, and final review before submit."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Order status is one of Received, Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered, Cancelled, visible to both customer and staff."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each status change records status, date/time, and the user or system that made the change, forming a visible timeline."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can edit quantities, remove lines, and (where permitted) change delivery date/address/note on an order that is still Received (before confirmation)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff confirming an order validates product availability and customer info, locks it from customer cancellation, sets status Confirmed, records who/when, and sends the customer a confirmation email (noting any staff-made quantity changes)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff rejecting an order sets it to Cancelled, records reason/who/when, and notifies the customer."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Status changing to Out for delivery triggers an email to the customer identifying the order."},{"kind":"error","text":"Staff cannot edit an order that has already moved past Confirmed (e.g. already Picking/Delivered) through the normal edit action."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only office staff/admin can change order status or edit orders; customers cannot."}],"id":"I-14","readingChosen":"Orders move through a fixed status lifecycle (Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for delivery→Delivered, or Cancelled) with a recorded timeline; staff can edit/confirm/reject only up to the point confirmation locks the order."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer views a list of their company's past orders with number, date, delivery date, address, total, status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer opens an order detail page showing full line items, prices, totals, note, and status timeline."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer cancels an order while its status is Received; status becomes Cancelled and is recorded in the timeline."},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer attempting to cancel an order no longer in Received status is blocked and told to contact the distributor office."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer clicks 'repeat order' on a past order: previously ordered products that are still active/available are added to a new basket, unavailable products are flagged, and prices are recalculated using the customer's current price list."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can adjust quantities in the repeated-order basket before going through normal checkout; no new order is created until the customer completes checkout and submits."}],"id":"I-15","readingChosen":"Customers can view their order history, cancel an order only while it is in Received status, and repeat a past order by loading its lines into a new basket for review/checkout (not auto-submit)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"When an order's status changes to Delivered, the system automatically creates an invoice with invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, date, lines, quantities, prices, total, and payment status Unpaid."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer views their invoices list and opens invoice detail; buyer cannot view another customer's invoices."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer downloads an invoice as a PDF containing billing and order information."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff view any customer's invoices."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff mark an invoice as paid, recording payment date and the user who recorded it; invoice status updates to Paid."},{"kind":"data","text":"Invoice status can be Paid, Unpaid, or Overdue, with Overdue derived automatically based on configured ageing rules."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only staff/admin can mark invoices as paid; customers cannot change invoice payment status."}],"id":"I-16","readingChosen":"Invoices are auto-generated when an order reaches Delivered; customers/staff can view and download them as PDF; staff can mark invoices paid and record payment date, driving payment-status display."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin adds, edits, and retires a product, including category assignment, manufacturer info, product codes, and compatibility data; retired products remain in historical orders."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin uploads a product image; invalid file type or oversized file is rejected with an error message; admin can replace an existing image."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin creates, edits, and retires categories, and reassigns products between categories."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin invites a new user (buyer, account manager, or staff) by entering their details; user receives an invitation email, sets a password, and account becomes active."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin deactivates a user, reactivates a user where permitted, and changes a user's role or company association."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin creates/edits/renames a price list, sets/edits/removes product prices within it, assigns it to a customer, and deactivates a price list."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only administrators can access product, category, user, and price-list management screens; staff and customers cannot."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to invite a user with an already-registered email or deactivate a non-existent user returns a validation error rather than succeeding silently."}],"id":"I-17","readingChosen":"Admin screens cover CRUD/management for products (incl. images, categories, compatibility), users (invite/deactivate/reactivate/role-change), categories, and price lists (create/edit/assign/deactivate)."}]},{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can sign in and place an order entirely through the web portal without contacting office staff by phone or email."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Office staff can still create an order on behalf of a customer who phones in, as a fallback channel."},{"kind":"data","text":"System records whether an order was placed by the customer or created by staff on their behalf."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Customer without an active account cannot place orders through the portal and must be invited first."}],"id":"I-1","readingChosen":"Portal replaces phone/email ordering as the primary channel for placing orders; customers self-serve instead of calling/emailing office staff."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Searching by product name returns matching products including partial matches."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Searching by product code or manufacturer part number returns matching products including partial matches."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Searching by manufacturer/brand returns matching products."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Selecting a category filters the catalogue to that category; customer can change or clear the selected category."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Selecting vehicle attributes (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) returns only products marked compatible with that vehicle."},{"kind":"error","text":"Search with no matches returns an empty result with no products shown (no error thrown)."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Catalogue browsing and search are only visible to signed-in customers (no public anonymous search)."}],"id":"I-2","readingChosen":"Catalogue supports search/filter by part number, product name, category, and vehicle info, returning matching products."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Product listings and product detail pages show the price from the customer's assigned price list, not a generic price."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Product listings and product detail pages show a stock status (in stock, low stock, out of stock) derived from the latest successful ERP import."},{"kind":"permission","text":"A customer can never see another customer's pricing."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a product has no price in the customer's assigned price list, the product's price cannot be displayed as a valid price (must be flagged/handled, not shown as zero or wrong price)."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the latest ERP stock import failed, the portal continues showing the last successfully imported stock status rather than blank/incorrect data."}],"id":"I-3","readingChosen":"Pricing and stock shown to a customer reflect their assigned price list and the latest imported stock data, hidden from other customers."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Orders placed by customers online flow directly into the staff order queue without staff re-keying order details."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can still create an order manually on behalf of a customer via a guided flow (select customer, address, products, quantities) when needed."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff order creation flow shows customer-specific pricing automatically rather than requiring manual price lookup."}],"id":"I-4","readingChosen":"Self-service ordering and staff-created orders reduce manual data entry for office staff compared to manual phone/email order entry."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can view a list of their company's orders with number, date, delivery date, address, total, and status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can view an order's detail page including status timeline with date/time and who/what performed each transition."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can view a list of invoices with payment status (paid/unpaid/overdue)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can download an invoice as a PDF."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Customer cannot view another customer's orders or invoices even via direct URL/ID manipulation."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to access an order/invoice not belonging to the customer returns an access-denied/not-found response."}],"id":"I-5","readingChosen":"Customers can view order status/timeline and invoices (including PDF) for their own company only."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can view all orders in a queue showing order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, total, and status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can filter the order queue by customer, date, and status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can open an order from the queue to view detail and perform permitted actions (confirm, reject, edit, update status)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can export the day's delivery list as a CSV containing order and address details needed by drivers."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Customer buyers and account managers cannot access the staff order queue or delivery export."}],"id":"I-6","readingChosen":"Staff get an order queue with filters, and a delivery list export for today's deliveries."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff dashboard shows counts/lists of new orders, orders awaiting confirmation, orders being picked, orders out for delivery, today's deliveries, and outstanding invoices."},{"kind":"error","text":"Staff dashboard surfaces failed ERP stock imports so staff are aware of data issues."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can view operational reports summarizing sales/product activity."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Customers cannot access staff/management reporting or dashboard."}],"id":"I-7","readingChosen":"Management (staff/admin) can view basic sales and product reporting via a dashboard/reports area."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Every order status transition is recorded with status, date/time, and the user or system that performed it, and this history is retained and viewable."},{"kind":"data","text":"Invoice payment recording stores payment date and the user who recorded it, and this is retained."},{"kind":"data","text":"Changes to customer accounts (e.g., price list assignment changes, address changes) are retained as history accessible to administrators."},{"kind":"data","text":"Catalogue changes (product edits, retirements, category changes, price list edits) are retained as history/audit log accessible to administrators."},{"kind":"data","text":"Retired products and deactivated users remain visible in historical orders/invoices rather than being deleted."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only administrators can view the administrative audit/history information."}],"id":"I-8","readingChosen":"System keeps an immutable audit trail of order status changes, invoice payment recording, customer account changes, and catalogue/price edits, viewable by admins."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"User signs in with email and password; correct credentials grant a session and access appropriate to their role."},{"kind":"error","text":"Incorrect credentials show an 'invalid credentials' message without revealing whether the email exists."},{"kind":"happy","text":"User can sign out, ending their session."},{"kind":"error","text":"After 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, the account is locked for 15 minutes and the user is told the account is temporarily locked."},{"kind":"error","text":"Login attempts during the lock period are blocked and the user is informed of the remaining lock state."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Successful sign-in after the lock period expires restores normal access."},{"kind":"happy","text":"User can request password reset via email; system sends a reset email; following the link lets the user set a new password and confirms the change; user can then sign in with the new password."},{"kind":"error","text":"Expired or invalid reset tokens are rejected with an error message."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin invites a user by entering details; invited user receives an email, sets a password via the invitation link, and their account becomes active."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Deactivated users cannot sign in and are told their account is inactive; they cannot place new orders."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Unauthenticated users attempting to access protected pages are redirected to sign-in / denied access."}],"id":"I-9","readingChosen":"Authentication covers sign-in, failed-login lockout, password reset via email link, invitation-based account creation, and deactivation."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer views a paginated/listable catalogue showing image, name, code, manufacturer, unit/pack size, price, stock status, and add-to-basket action per product."},{"kind":"